# The justified entries of the vocabulary of combinator properties
# (CombinatorPropertyVocabulary): for each property, the lemma a knowledge
# file must declare for a combinator C before it may declare the property
# of C. The file's one field is a Scott tuple of one member per property,
# in the order of CombinatorPropertyVocabulary's justifiedProperties, each
# member `λs. s Left Right`: the lemma's two sides, in either order, each a
# program whose first abstraction binds the combinator. No property is named
# in the file (https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1792; the user,
# 2026-11-20: "字符串是违规的").
#
#   - `associative`: C is associative; its lemma has the sides
#     λx. λy. λz. C x (C y z) and λx. λy. λz. C (C x y) z.
#   - `repeller`: C is the identity; its lemma, C's erasure, has the sides
#     λx. C x and λx. x.

λ export
. export
λ properties
. properties (λs. s (λc x y z. c x λ. c y z) λc x y z. c (c x y) z) λs. s (λc x. c x) λc x. x
